  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 73ff519377b990a4c81cd1461a3c1f62, type: 3}
  m_Name: Irah_W10_Teach
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::DialogueNode
  speakerName: Irah
  speakerPortrait: {fileID: 0}
  dialogueText: 'Adda dagiti oras a saan a makaanay ti simple a panagyaman tapno
    maipakita no kasano ti kaadu ti panagyamanmo.


    Iti Ilokano, ti ''agyamanak
    unay'' ket kayatna a saoen ti ''thank you very much.''


    Mabalinmo nga agusar
    iti daytoy no adda nangaramid iti naisangsangayan a naimbag wenno naindaklan
    a tulong kenka.


    Denggem a naimbag: agyamanak unay.


    Ita, padasem nga
    ibagam ti ''agyamanak unay'' iti bukodmo a timek.'
  translatedText: 'Sometimes a simple thank you isn''t enough to express how grateful
    you feel.

    In Ilokano, ''agyamanak unay'' means ''thank you very much.''

    You
    can use it when someone does something especially kind or generous for you.

    Now,
    try saying ''agyamanak unay'' yourself.'
